<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Central Bank of Ecuador</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1927–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Central Bank of Ecuador was founded in 1927 on the advice of the American economist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edwin-kemmerer">Edwin Kemmerer</a>, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julian-revolution">Julian Revolution</a> of 1925 had ended the dominance of the private banks of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guayaquil">Guayaquil</a> over money and credit. It issued the sucre until the currency crisis of 1999–2000, when Ecuador adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> dollar. It continues to manage the payments system and reserves.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/central-bank-of-ecuador.jpg" alt="Central Bank of Ecuador" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Banco Central del Ecuador · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logotipo_del_Banco_Central_del_Ecuador.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
